I think the point he was trying to make wasn't that we should make a new 
scoring system. I think it was that there's no possible way to 
programatically access how well someone is playing. As you've pointed 
out yourself, people play differently. Making a scoring method that 
wouldn't give advantage to one style of play over another is impossible, 
as far as I can see. I think that's more or less what he was saying.


